  "sourceUrl": "https://www.4gon.co.uk/engenius-neutron-ews-48port-managed-gigabit-410w-poe-switch-ews7952p-p-7485.html",
  "notes": "The page gives the port census three times over and they agree: '10/100/1000 Base-T, POE+: 48', '10/100/1000 SFP Ports: 4', '1 x RJ45 Console Port'. So 48 copper PoE+ ports, **4 gigabit SFP** (100/1000, not 10G - the marketing bullet says '1-10 Gbps SFP+ Slots', which the specification table contradicts, and the table wins), and a separate console. The PoE numbers are the useful part and they are all quoted: 802.3at/af on ports **1-48**, **30 W** per port, and a **410 W total budget** - less than 48 x 30 W, so 13 ports at full 30 W exhausts it, which is exactly the arithmetic a lab should be able to discover. Full-load consumption is 509 W against a 100-240 VAC input. Managed Layer 2 only: no `l3-forward`, since this is a switch with VLAN routing rather than a router."
